# Who may authorise a quorum-controlled action.
#
# design/03-identity-and-access.md:
#
#     The following require two approvals from {Jamie, Wayne, Art}, with
#     requester and approvers being distinct people:
#       - kms:ScheduleKeyDeletion
#       - Backup vault deletion or vault lock modification
#       - Removal of a member account from the Organization
#       - Disabling CloudTrail or the Config recorder
#
# Atlassian accountIds, not email addresses. The accountId is what the approval
# records carry and it is stable across a name or address change; an email
# address is neither. Find one at:
#
#   https://<site>.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/myself           (your own)
#   scripts/jira-check.sh                                     (reports it)
#
# Copy this file to config/quorum.env and fill it in. That file is gitignored:
# an accountId identifies an individual and does not belong in the repository.
# Publish to SSM with scripts/sync-quorum-approvers.sh.

# One line per person. The comment is for whoever edits this file; only the
# accountId is published.
QUORUM_APPROVER_1=""      # Jamie
QUORUM_APPROVER_2=""      # Wayne
QUORUM_APPROVER_3=""      # Art
QUORUM_APPROVER_4=""      # Tina -- quorum set widened to all four partners, D-022

# How many distinct approvals a quorum action requires.
#
# Two, per design 03. Do not lower this to make a deployment proceed -- the
# whole value of the control is that it cannot be satisfied by one person, and
# a pipeline that refuses because only one approver exists is working, not
# broken. Raise it if the partner set grows and the risk appetite changes.
QUORUM_MINIMUM_APPROVALS="2"
